In .NET 10, `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` is deprecated (Android removed it in API 30+). MAUI now uses **edge-to-edge** rendering by default. Here's the modern fix:

## Option 1: Use `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` (simplest)

MAUI 10 includes automatic keyboard-avoidance scrolling. Ensure it's not disabled:

```csharp
// In MauiProgram.cs — this is ON by default, just don't disable it
builder.UseMauiApp<App>();
```

If you previously disabled it, remove:
```csharp
KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect(); // remove this
```

## Option 2: Wrap your page in a `ScrollView`

`KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` works best when the focused input is inside a `ScrollView`:

```xml
<ContentPage>
  <Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">
    <ScrollView Grid.Row="0">
      <!-- Chat messages -->
    </ScrollView>

    <Grid Grid.Row="1">
      <Entry Placeholder="Type a message..." />
    </Grid>
  </Grid>
</ContentPage>
```

## Option 3: Android-specific inset handling (full control)

In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    // Set soft input mode to adjust nothing (we handle it manually)
    Window!.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(false);

    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window.DecorView, new InsetsListener());
}

private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        // imeInsets.Bottom gives keyboard height in pixels
        v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, imeInsets.Bottom);
        return insets;
    }
}
```

## TL;DR

- **Don't** set `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` — it's a no-op now.
- **Do** rely on MAUI's built-in `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` (enabled by default) and ensure your input is in a scrollable layout.
- For precise control on Android, use the `WindowInsetsCompat` API to read IME height and apply padding.
